<title>USA: Clinton repeats call for campaign finance reform.</title>
<headline>Clinton repeats call for campaign finance reform.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Bill Clinton on Friday repeated his call for campaign finance reform, saying he would do &quot;whatever is necessary&quot; to pass such legislation.</p>
<p>&quot;Now is the time for bipartisan campaign finance reform legislation,&quot; Clinton told a news conference, adding that he supported the existing McCain-Feingold campaign finance reform bill and would seek to pass it as soon as possible, with an ammendment banning contributions from non-citizens.</p>
</text>
